      <h2 class="eyebrow-title">The problem with standard training</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="split">
      <div class="split__col lift reveal">
        <h3>The problem</h3>
        <p>Most corporate courses follow a program designed for anyone, and therefore for no one in particular.</p>
        <ul class="crosslist">
          <li>Examples on made-up data, far from daily work</li>
          <li>People at very different levels in the same room</li>
          <li>Lots of theory, little practice</li>
          <li>The day after, nobody knows where to start</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="split__col split__col--accent spot reveal">
        <h3>Our approach</h3>
        <p>We treat training as a project: with a business goal, a measured starting level and an expected outcome.</p>
        <ul class="checklist">
          <li>Exercises built on your real files and processes</li>
          <li>Groups split by level after an initial assessment</li>
          <li>Goals agreed with the team manager</li>
          <li>Materials, recordings and support after the course</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

